_site/
.quarto/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
.DS_Store

# Source PDFs must never be committed (docs/data-strategy.md)
*.pdf

# models.json is generated at build time from models.yaml
models.json

/.quarto/
**/*.quarto_ipynb

# Quarto build artifacts
_freeze/

# Never commit credentials
*apikey*
*api_key*
.env
secrets.*

# Review overlays are drawn ON TOP OF the source page image, so they ARE the
# copyrighted figure. They exist only to be looked at once by the maintainer in
# a private artifact, and must never enter this public repository - every data
# sidecar's redistribution_basis says the figure image is not reproduced.
# Everything under review/, not just the images. An extraction CSV sitting there
# is a dataset that has NOT been through the maintainer's visual review, and
# committing one would publish unreviewed numbers with no provenance sidecar -
# the same failure as committing the overlay, one step removed. Caught on H1.4,
# 2026-07-31, where fig4_digitised.csv matched no pattern.
#
# A reviewed dataset does not live here: it moves into <page>/data/ with its
# .meta.yaml sidecar, and that path is tracked.
# Ignore the CONTENTS, not the directory: git will not re-include a file inside
# an ignored directory, so `queue_cases/*/review/` would make the negations below
# dead letters.
queue_cases/*/review/*
!queue_cases/*/review/*.md
!queue_cases/*/review/*.py

# The same images base64-inlined. `scripts/dashboards.py --with-images` writes
# the maintainer's private copy here; the tracked docs/dashboards/*.html are
# built without images and name the overlays instead.
docs/dashboards/private/
